!Sample_data_processing = Base Calling with RTA2 run with default parameters: "The NextSeq 500 uses an implementation of Real-Time Analysis (RTA) software called RTA2. RTA2 runs on the instrument computer and extracts intensities from images, performs base calling, and assigns a quality score to the base call."
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were filtered / timmed with fastx 0.0.14 with parameters: fastx_trimmer -v -f 9 -l 75 | fastq_quality_trimmer -v -t 20 -l 1 | fastq_quality_filter -v -q 30 -p 75
!Sample_data_processing = tRNA and rRNA treads where filtered out by mapping on a tRNA / rRNA mini-genome with Bowtie 2.3.3 with parameters bowtie2 -t --fast -p 16 -x /<path>/human_rRNA_tRNA_index | samtools view -b -f 4 | bedtools bamtofastq -i
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were mapped with Tophat 2.1.1 with parameters: --library-type fr-firststrand --b2-sensitive -i 30 -m 1 -g 10 --max-coverage-intron 1000000 -G <path>/gencode.v23.chr_patch_hapl_scaff.annotation_appris_principal.gtf
!Sample_data_processing = Mapped reads were counted with HTSeq-count  0.9.1 with parameters : -f sam -s reverse -a 10 -t exon -i gene_id -m union
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: An Excel .xlsx file containing a matrix of raw counts, as provided by HTSeq-count, for all samples.
!Sample_platform_id = GPL18573
